  "identifier": "DHSVM",
  "title": "Distributed Hydrology Soil Vegetation Model",
  "description": {
    "en": "DHSVM numerically represents with high spatial resolution (typically on the order of 100 m) the effects of local weather, topography, soil type, and vegetation on the hydrology within watersheds. The model is used to study the impacts of climate change, land use change, forest management practices, flooding, glacier dynamics, stream temperature and stream quality."
